From df4a285097a24a62f8e71b38e90eae0e33ed100d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:55:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: replace serde_norway with serde-saphyr

serde_norway 0.9.42, like the serde_yaml it forks, fails to compile once Cargo's lint cap is lifted: its libyaml
binding creates nine references through raw pointers (dangerous_implicit_autorefs). serde-saphyr is a pure-Rust
reader that forbids unsafe code. codex only reads YAML, so codex-skills now provides from_yaml_str and
from_yaml_slice, configured with the YAML 1.2 rules serde_yaml applied: only true and false are booleans, and
numbers written with leading zeros or underscores stay strings. Untyped frontmatter becomes a serde_json::Value.
